Circle (smooth cylinder section)
# Unit-diameter circle: the 2D section of a smooth sphere, and the control
# case for golfball.dat -- same circle, same node count, no dimples.
# Node order matches the Selig convention used by the NACA samples:
#   TE (theta=0) -> upper surface -> LE (theta=pi) -> lower surface -> TE.
# Has an exact analytic solution, Cp = 1 - 4 sin^2(theta), which the panel
# method reproduces to machine precision when these nodes are used directly
# (re-paneling onto cosine spacing costs a few percent at the shoulders).
# NOTE: a bluff body in an inviscid panel method has no drag and no wake.
# Comparing Cd with golfball.dat shows why dimples need a viscous model:
# both are ~0 here, because d'Alembert does not care about dimples.
